1	1	SLA_REC_RAMP	0.5	9
1	1	SLA_REC_THR	0.0	9
# Data record 20261110 revision 14 (2026-11-25): revision 9 with the data sheet of 2026-11-25 (new packs, see the top of the file).
# SLA_MASS, SLA_CG_X, EKF2_IMU_POS_X (IMU 8 mm aft of the CG) and SLA_I_* (CAD, rotated as before) from the sheet; SLA_EDF_T1..T4 linear to
# the bench 4.402 kg (43.17 N) at 42 V. Pitch and yaw moment derivatives, uncertainties and M_SCALE x 0.98633 (canard arm 0.16373 / 0.166);
# RATE_P and RATE_I x I_new / I_old / that factor and SP_ACC x the inverse, so every loop keeps its design crossover (roll I x 1.1195,
# pitch x 1.2788, yaw x 1.2819). Roll moments and all forces do not depend on the CG and are unchanged. Not measured. See SLAAPS_DATA_RECORD.md.
# Data record 20261110 revision 9 (2026-11-23): revision 7 with the body correction (modeled, slender-body theory, 85 mm body at the
# canards): canard derivatives, their uncertainties, SLA_x_M_SCALE and SP_ACC x 2.30 in pitch and yaw and x 2.95 in roll; RATE_P and
# RATE_I divided by the same factors, so the design crossover is kept for the stronger canards. Not measured. See SLAAPS_DATA_RECORD.md.
# Revision 7: revision 3 (wind tunnel 18-40 m/s: modeled derivatives, moment scales and rate gains at 40 m/s)
# with the weighed mass 1.979 kg (2026-11-23; was the CAD 2.05 kg). The CG 0.233 m was confirmed by the same check.
# Incomplete until the project lead declares it Calibrated (SLA_DATA_STATE 1). Revision 2 (measured data) was declared
# Calibrated by the project lead, Kael Spry, 2026-11-12; revision 3 changes only modeled values; revision 7 only SLA_MASS.
# SLA_Cn_ZERO stay 0 here by the lead's choice; canards are trimmed manually on the board after loading this file.
# Revision 1 was declared Calibrated by the project lead, Kael Spry, 2026-11-10.
# See docs/SLAAPS_DATA_RECORD.md for what it covers; modeled values stay modeled.
1	1	SLA_DATA_REC	20261110	6
1	1	SLA_DATA_REV	14	6
1	1	SLA_DATA_STATE	0	6
